{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire","id":1345048,"title":"Starting Mage vs Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-31T13:57:17-07:00","id":1345048,"title":"Starting Mage vs Vampire","content":"OK, I am sure it has been asked before, but my search-fu has failed me. Other than not be in the same city with them, what is the best way for a fresh out of the box Mage to deal with a hostile vampire? Straight chargen, no additional XP. How would you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25758-vandarl","name":"Vandarl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:20:41-07:00","id":1345057,"title":"","content":"There's a bunch of different ways, really it depends on what you want to do.<br /> <br /> You could literally just build mundane skills to the point where you are the perfect vampire slayer. Get access to any sort of fire based weaponry (Dragon breath shotgun rounds, explosive incendiary rounds, etc [These are hard to get but some points in contacts/allies/make them yourself is a way around it, all mundane]) At that point you can use your magick to just make yourself better at what you already do. Entropy for aiming/dodging/hitting weakspots, life for healing yourself. Maybe use life/mind/something to have a 'snap out of it' effect trigger if you get bit and your willpower isn't high enough to resist. Forces 2 to increase velocity on bullets for damage, or just do forces damage in general.<br /> You can try using a crossbow to stake them but the DC is kinda high but using magick you could lower it and pretty easily sling some stakes into some hearts. I think the DC is default....8? 7? So with a max of -3 you're shooting at DC 4 and need to do like 3 levels of damage. Not impossible but not nearly as good if there are multiple vampires. (Unless you use like, correspondence 4 to make the stakes hit all vampires at the same time but that isn't a starting character. Now you could probably use matter or some shit to make copies of the stake mid air but this is getting complicated so lets move on)<br /> <br /> You could focus completely on magick. Arete 3, Forces 3, Prime 2. Bam, fireball. If they don't frenzy they are dead next turn because of all the damage they just took (Your follow up attack could basically be anything, as the vampire will be fleeing. If they aren't fleeing they will be so weak their dice pool is fucked. So if they aren't fleeing, just go curb stomp it to death. If they are, just shoot them or something. Getting in their direct path means they can attack you. Any ST who has a fire frenzy vampire rush towards you is doing the frenzy rules differently so this doesn't apply.)<br /> <br /> Problems include: Celerity + dodge will fuck you up. Because fireballs are dodged by using the arete roll, that means every dodge success they get nullifies some of your potential damage (I swear to god if ya'll start screaming at me about some house rules about using wits + occult to aim fireballs I'll fireball this metaphorical building we are discussing in. The default rules for 'magick attacks without a weapon directing them' are pretty shitty.) <br /> You can help nullify this by using a weapon of sorts, as then it becomes a matter of doding a dexterity + weapon roll, which makes the likely hood you get atleast one success higher. It also doesn't matter if you get 1 success to hit with a magick damage attack or 50, the damage is the same.<br /> <br /> After that...it's really just flavor/what you feel like doing. No starting mage can really make sunlight out of nothing (Requires some shit like forces 5 + maybe optional spirit 5 if your ST hates you) or requires like Correspondence -something- and Forces -whatever- to teleport sunlight to you, but it's a lot of effort for something you can mimic with good old fire.<br /> <br /> Mind effects are worthless if your ST uses HDYDT don't even try. The Difficulty will be far too high.<br /> <br /> <br /> For added help:<br /> <br /> Take some combination of flaws + merits and work with your ST to establish you have no blood in your body and are basically immune to the kiss. Immortal of some variant would probably do the trick.<br /> Familiars of some kind would be helpful, especially if it's an elemental that can't be bit. ESPECIALLY IF IT'S FIRE.<br /> <br /> Werewolf allies is like a 3 point merit.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk is a merit.<br /> <br /> Kung-fu/Do is decent if you have it so you are doing lethal damage with your hits. If you are doing bashing, I don't recommend it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T01:28:22-07:00","id":1345180,"title":"","content":"Arguably the best way to &quot;beat&quot; a hostile vampire is to avoid them entirely. Keep the leech at a distance, where their powers are less effective. Although when I say &quot;distance&quot;, I mean less in the sense of physical distance (although Correspondence can work wonders with the right conjunctional Spheres), and more in the sense of avoiding a fight in the first place.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, the first dot in every Sphere is sensory in nature (barring some exceptions like Mind), and being able to pick out the vampire before the vampire notices you is important. Luckily, Mages &quot;read&quot; as normal mortals to vampire senses, save when they are actively using magick (and then only if the vampire happens to be using Aura Sense at the time). Whereas a vampire sets off magickal senses in multiple different ways. If the two don't already know about each other (by face and/or name), and you plopped them both down in a busy club, the Mage would notice the Vampire way before the reverse. Giving the Mage time to do whatever they needed to do to prepare, whether that means setting up an ambush, creating distractions, siccing some other party onto the vampire, or escaping/hiding. Simply having that much advance warning can be critical.<br /> <br /> Indeed, that's sort of the advantage Mages have against Vampires in a nutshell. Give a Mage time to prepare, and they can accomplish just about anything.<br /> <br /> From there, it depends on 1) what Spheres you spec into, and 2) what your goals are in relation to the vampire.<br /> <br /> If you want to destroy the vampire, Jihelu has already suggested many options. Magick that enhances mundane weapons/abilities. Out-lasting the vampire with Life. Good old fashioned FIRE. Other options include slowing the leech down with Time (or speeding yourself up), teleporting in yourself and/or weapons with Correspondence, turning the environment into hazards with Matter (air to acid, entangling their clothes, impale with concrete spikes, etc). Spirit can get Umbrood on your side, which can make a vampire's unlife an unliving hell, while Mind can forge illusions (you can also use Forces) or protect against certain vampire powers. Prime can also be used as a blunt, Vulgar method of getting vamps off your back; either &quot;Rub the Bones&quot; (Prime 2) or outright attacking with Aggravated damage weapons of pure Quintessence.<br /> <br /> If you just want to avoid being destroyed (with or without counter attacking), Forces can make you invisible or forge illusions to trick the vampire. It's also great for erecting walls of fire, that make most vampires consider a mage more trouble than they're worth. Assuming the ST doesn't make Mind useless against Night Folk (thanks HDYDT), you can erect an &quot;Ignore Me!&quot; field that makes the Mage of little interest to the leech. It could also make the mage attract mortals, keeping a thick wall of people between the mage and the vamp (rendering it dangerous to risk the Masquerade or police action by attacking openly). Time can let the Mage know when the vampire is coming, or where they've been, so the two characters never need be in the same place at the same time. Forces, Mind, and Life (and arguably Prime, with Body of Light) give the Mage options for appearing like someone else, so they can walk around even when the vamp knows their face. If all else fails, the mage can always teleport away with Correspondence.<br /> <br /> What can be trickier is when the vamp doesn't attack personally, but instead uses intermediaries. Using Influence and mind powers to &quot;attack&quot; the Mage through institutions, or sending Ghouls or mind-controlled assailants to rough the Mage up. The Spheres can still help, just with an eye for the indirect moves. Anything that lets a Mage avoid being found by a vampire can work on a Ghoul, and Aura Reading (as supplied by Mind 1 or Spirit 1) can still pick out Ghouls by the pale patches in their auras. Entropy can be used more abstractly to make the systems of government and business work more efficiently in the Mage's favor (a bureaucracy is just a machine made of people and paperwork, so Entropy 3 should arguably apply).<br /> <br /> Going away from the Spheres themselves, the Arcane background can work wonders at making a Mage harder to find, by basically everyone. High levels can be a double edged sword, of course, but even small amounts can help a willworker squeak by unnoticed by all but the most dedicated and perceptive of undead assailants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T06:07:12-07:00","id":1345211,"title":"","content":"Lots of good ideas. But i think this will depend strongly of what clan and disciplines the vampire has. Does he has Fortitude? Celerity? Potence? Dominate?<br /> <br /> Of fourse, the best plan, as bluecho posted, is to avlid being detected and ambush the vampire. <br /> But in direct confrontation, vulgar Forces attacks with WP points for 1 extra succes is the best option.<br /> Now, what happened to rolling Arete and dealing damage? All spells need an sttack roll now? How the hell you dodge a lightning bolt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T08:11:09-07:00","id":1345236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can try using a crossbow to stake them but the DC is kinda high but using magick you could lower it and pretty easily sling some stakes into some hearts. I think the DC is default....8? 7? So with a max of -3 you're shooting at DC 4 and need to do like 3 levels of damage. Not impossible but not nearly as good if there are multiple vampires. (Unless you use like, correspondence 4 to make the stakes hit all vampires at the same time but that isn't a starting character. Now you could probably use matter or some shit to make copies of the stake mid air but this is getting complicated so lets move on)</div> </div> </div> </div>A way to enhance this strategy could be to make the stake cause Aggravated (Prime 2). That way it's harder to resist (and easier to get 3 levels in). You may end killing the vampire, but that sure beats having the vampire retaliate, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> For the multiple target issue.<br /> 1rst. Ask yourself:<i> what I'm doing figthing multiple vampires all by myself with a crossbow?.</i> If it's unavoidable, you flee, Invisibility or teleportation are your friends.<br /> If you <i>really </i>want to do this (Not the best strategy, to. But for the lulz), and you happen to have Time 3, you could remember that it doesn't just give you extra actions, it can also make everything faster: thus increasing the &quot;fire ratio&quot; of a crossbow it's super vulgar, but doable. I really don't recomend this, though.<br /> <br /> Note that not everyone knows that staking a vampire doesn't kill them outright - that we know doesn't mean that the mage should know, so this could return to bit her in the ass (or elsewhere)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the hell you dodge a lightning bolt?</div> </div> </div> </div>By shouting to the sky: &quot;it's the rules, it's the rules!. And its difficulty 6, that's in the rules toooo!&quot;. XD<br /> <br /> To be fair, if a mage it's pointing a wand at you, you really should move from the way. I would rule that the dodge it's possible depending on how it's casted (I.E: From a wand, it's like dodging bullets. From the stormy sky and directed to you as the consequence of a silent curse or some science stuff, nope, you don't get to dodge unless you have Goku levels of Celerity)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-01-2019, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:15:08-07:00","id":1345254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vandarl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire#post1345048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than not be in the same city with them, what is the best way for a fresh out of the box Mage to deal with a hostile vampire? Straight chargen, no additional XP. How would you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be interesting to know where this hypotetical mage stands. What's the situation and what counts as &quot;dealing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Are we talking of a mage that's gona be a vampire hunter, &quot;van helsing&quot; style?, or just a mage that has had or expects a problem with vampires and wants to come on top?<br /> <br /> A hunter would want to assasinate the vampire, but another mage could favor negotiating or focus on having countermeasures in case vampires attack (assuming hostility hasn't started yet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:21:15-07:00","id":1345256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345236#post1345236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By shouting to the sky: &quot;it's the rules, it's the rules!. And its difficulty 6, that's in the rules toooo!&quot;. XD<br /> <br /> To be fair, if a mage it's pointing a wand at you, you really should move from the way. I would rule that the dodge it's possible depending on how it's casted (I.E: From a wand, it's like dodging bullets. From the stormy sky and directed to you as the consequence of a silent curse or some science stuff, nope, you don't get to dodge unless you have Goku levels of Celerity)</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage can just gesture quickly and throw the fireball. Or zap the lightning palpatine style. <br /> The thing is, there are rules for using only Arete to deal damage, we should try to fit into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T11:33:33-07:00","id":1345284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345256#post1345256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, there are rules for using only Arete to deal damage, we should try to fit into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well.<br /> <br /> I think that weaving the correct instrument /practice one could make a case for those rules to be applied.<br /> <br /> For instance, a witch cursing *you* of all people (in a way that's evidently refering tou you, like, saying your name) it's not something that can be &quot;evaded&quot; by any logic or reason. It would be like trying to &quot;dodge&quot; an argument or an accusation (which can be done, but it's hardly a function of &quot;Athletics&quot;).<br /> <br /> So, you curse the vampire to catch fire. &quot;I curse thee, vile vampire, to burn with the fires of hell!&quot; (or something like that). No way &quot;I dodge&quot; can be a reasonable answer to a witch yelling that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:08:05-07:00","id":1345290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345284#post1345284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, well.<br /> <br /> I think that weaving the correct instrument /practice one could make a case for those rules to be applied.<br /> <br /> For instance, a witch cursing *you* of all people (in a way that's evidently refering tou you, like, saying your name) it's not something that can be &amp;quot;evaded&amp;quot; by any logic or reason. It would be like trying to &amp;quot;dodge&amp;quot; an argument or an accusation (which can be done, but it's hardly a function of &amp;quot;Athletics&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> So, you curse the vampire to catch fire. &amp;quot;I curse thee, vile vampire, to burn with the fires of hell!&amp;quot; (or something like that). No way &amp;quot;I dodge&amp;quot; can be a reasonable answer to a witch yelling that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're talking about spontaneous combustion? Wouldn't the mage need Matter 2 to do that on a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:27:11-07:00","id":1345299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345290#post1345290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you're talking about spontaneous combustion? Wouldn't the mage need Matter 2 to do that on a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>To cause the physical cells to combust? Yes. To ignite the air around the target? No. <br /> <br /> However this is a lot of purple paradigm talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:34:06-07:00","id":1345306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345290#post1345290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you're talking about spontaneous combustion? Wouldn't the mage need Matter 2 to do that on a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>IF the ST says that grabbing the Pattern of the target it's needed for the Effect <i>as described</i> then <i>we're done</i>.<br /> <br /> Life 3/Matter 2-3 would be the least we would need to add to do it. Because &quot;vampires&quot; are a pattern of Life/Matter combined (neither one nor the other), and one needs Life 3 to affect others in any way. Advantage being that's now completely undodgeable, armor won't block it (arguaby not even natural armor), and Prime/Quintessence may not be needed because we can fuel the effect <i>with the vampire</i> <i>(if using Matter 3)</i>.<br /> <br /> This is a bit iffy, though. One doesn't need Life to make a human levitate, unless one want's to lock the effect. I think it can be argued that one doesn't need to add anything to materialize fire on &quot;someone&quot; rather than &quot;someplace&quot;, as long as that &quot;someone&quot; it's present and we can concentrate on her/him. As per <i>Dwight's</i> example, the fire itself needs not to come from the undead Pattern (it's just <i>targeted </i>at it, which it's different).<br /> <br /> Alas, it can be argued otherwise. I think the ST has rigth to say that if you want to cast in a way that the effect isn't separable from your target, you need the Spheres to affect the target directly. And since this way of casting IT'S strictly better than just summoning fire on the place, from a &quot;mechanic&quot; perspective it may makes sense to need to be more powerful to get that extra advantage we're looking for.<br /> <br /> One can also cause direct pattern damage to vampires with Life 3/Matter 3, that can't be dodged. We loose the &quot;fire&quot; property and that sweet extra success from Forces, though (and it requires a very dedicated build)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-01-2019, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T13:23:02-07:00","id":1345318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345299#post1345299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To cause the physical cells to combust? Yes. To ignite the air around the target? No. <br /> <br /> However this is a lot of purple paradigm talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ignite the air around hom wouldn't the rules of fire hazard apply instead of the Aretex2 damage? I mean, after the fire is created, it is no longer magick and regular fire rules apply, just like if you blowed a fireball and set fire on some object..<br /> <br /> And wouldn't that leave room for the vampire to dodge, since you're aiming at his position?<br /> Even better couldn't the vampire just take 3 steps in any direction and run away from the air ignited (of course he would take some dmg in the process).<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> your levitation example makes sense. You should be able to set someone on fire without Life, we are not changing nor locking patterns. In this case you could alter the voltage between you and the vampire and make a lightning bolt fly straight to him, this way he couldn't avoid the damage by walking like I posted before. Don't know if regular lightning damage should apply, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-01-2019, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T15:19:38-07:00","id":1345336,"title":"","content":"I'm going to snap my fingers and ignite every air molecule around your body in an instant, where is there to dodge?<br /> <br /> Now provided you survive my fiery assault and didn't R\u00f6tschreck as a result of above feel free to use blood to boost your strength or get automatic potenc successes and beat my mortal shell into a plulp, remember you can fill up afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 11-01-2019, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T22:45:02-07:00","id":1345388,"title":"","content":"M20 does suggest being able to do an awareness roll to dodge an attack that isn't exactly noticeable, but the rules are vague. Is the awareness roll the actual dodge or do I roll awareness + some other mental stat DC -whatever- and the shit ton of successes I get basically count for nothing because I just need 1 for &quot;Alright you have permission to dodge&quot;. So it's either: I get 4 successes on an awareness + stat roll to notice they are casting a spell that will beat my ass and those successes count as my dodge, or I get a weird reflexive roll that only needs 1 success for my ST to look at me and go &quot;HMMMMM you may dodge&quot;.<br /> Not sure of a solution.<br /> <br /> If you're thinking 'how would you dodge X' the example the book gives is literally someone spouting off a death curse and someone using awareness to notice something fucked is about to happen and dodging it. I can't think of anything more vague than 'Alright he's saying mean words, I've got a bad fucking feeling about this. Imma do a sick dodge to the side to hopefully dodge this'.<br /> <br /> There is also the issue I mentioned before with dodging attacks with no attack roll. I think the base assumption without rules is you roll against their arete roll, which means attacking without an attack roll sucks. If you use a laser gun compared to a staff and shoot at a vampire, and they get three successes on their dodge, we get a scenario like this:<br /> <br /> Laser gun: 8 (3 successes) Aggravated damage, 4 successes to hit.<br /> Vampire: 3 successes to dodge.<br /> Results: Vampire takes the full damage.<br /> <br /> Fireball: 8 (3 successes) Aggravated damage, no roll to hit.<br /> Vampire: 3 successes to dodge.<br /> Results: You subtract the dodge successes from the fireball, potentially making it do no damage or very little.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Use a laser gun or house rules (Occult + Manipulation is common as fuck) to avoid this kinda scenario.<br /> <br /> The above is how I'm pretty sure the scenario works, but it may not be. I don't think I've ever seen a FAQ or developer give an explanation for how the fuck, in M20, an attack roll works for a magick attack. I think it just hits and it's up to them to not be shitty and dodge. (I mean in regards to an attack roll with no discernible 'weapon', like a lasergun. That shit is easily in the text)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also a vampire surviving a fire attack is a win win no matter what. They either<br /> <br /> A: Frenzy, and run like hell. Leaving you free to beat their ass from afar.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> B: They didn't frenzy, and they are now hurt as fuck. Their dice pool is shit as hell and I don't think they can spend blood to nullify it (Can they?), meaning I can beat their butt.<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> C: They dodged my attack and I get my ass /beat/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 11-02-2019, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T14:04:31-07:00","id":1345472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345336#post1345336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to snap my fingers and ignite every air molecule around your body in an instant, where is there to dodge?<br /> <br /> Now provided you survive my fiery assault and didn't R\u00f6tschreck as a result of above feel free to use blood to boost your strength or get automatic potenc successes and beat my mortal shell into a plulp, remember you can fill up afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you think of my post above about it being regular fire then? Maybe this way the damage wouldn't be Arete x 2...<br /> And the vampire would just run away from the fire before dying (again).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T14:10:47-07:00","id":1345473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345388#post1345388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 does suggest being able to do an awareness roll to dodge an attack that isn't exactly noticeable, but the rules are vague. Is the awareness roll the actual dodge or do I roll awareness + some other mental stat DC -whatever- and the shit ton of successes I get basically count for nothing because I just need 1 for &amp;quot;Alright you have permission to dodge&amp;quot;. So it's either: I get 4 successes on an awareness + stat roll to notice they are casting a spell that will beat my ass and those successes count as my dodge, or I get a weird reflexive roll that only needs 1 success for my ST to look at me and go &amp;quot;HMMMMM you may dodge&amp;quot;.<br /> Not sure of a solution.<br /> <br /> If you're thinking 'how would you dodge X' the example the book gives is literally someone spouting off a death curse and someone using awareness to notice something fucked is about to happen and dodging it. I can't think of anything more vague than 'Alright he's saying mean words, I've got a bad fucking feeling about this. Imma do a sick dodge to the side to hopefully dodge this'.<br /> <br /> There is also the issue I mentioned before with dodging attacks with no attack roll. I think the base assumption without rules is you roll against their arete roll, which means attacking without an attack roll sucks. If you use a laser gun compared to a staff and shoot at a vampire, and they get three successes on their dodge, we get a scenario like this:<br /> <br /> Laser gun: 8 (3 successes) Aggravated damage, 4 successes to hit.<br /> Vampire: 3 successes to dodge.<br /> Results: Vampire takes the full damage.<br /> <br /> Fireball: 8 (3 successes) Aggravated damage, no roll to hit.<br /> Vampire: 3 successes to dodge.<br /> Results: You subtract the dodge successes from the fireball, potentially making it do no damage or very little.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Use a laser gun or house rules (Occult + Manipulation is common as fuck) to avoid this kinda scenario.<br /> <br /> The above is how I'm pretty sure the scenario works, but it may not be. I don't think I've ever seen a FAQ or developer give an explanation for how the fuck, in M20, an attack roll works for a magick attack. I think it just hits and it's up to them to not be shitty and dodge. (I mean in regards to an attack roll with no discernible 'weapon', like a lasergun. That shit is easily in the text)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also a vampire surviving a fire attack is a win win no matter what. They either<br /> <br /> A: Frenzy, and run like hell. Leaving you free to beat their ass from afar.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> B: They didn't frenzy, and they are now hurt as fuck. Their dice pool is shit as hell and I don't think they can spend blood to nullify it (Can they?), meaning I can beat their butt.<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> C: They dodged my attack and I get my ass /beat/</div> </div> </div> </div>As I see, this rule just allows the target to dodge, no success is carried.<br /> <br /> Where does M20 says about dodging curses?lol<br /> <br /> There is a FAQ in Book of secrets and it talks about magick combat, but ir doesn't answer our questions. In it, it seems that all magickal attacks need an attack roll to hit.<br /> <br /> Yet, in M20 page 417 we have the &quot;openly magickal&quot; atrsck, that is a vulgar spell that only rolls Arete and doesn't seems to allow dodge, in contrast to the &quot;focused magick&quot; that requires attack roll, allows dodge, but is often coincidental.<br /> <br /> The &quot;openly magickal&quot; says that you roll Arete to attack, but is implicit that the target isn't allowed to dodge. If that's the case you just roll Arete as an attack, and if you have more than 1 success, since your target won't dodge, you do direct damage, which is how we used to think it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T20:24:55-07:00","id":1345513,"title":"","content":"544, M20<br /> <br /> &quot;Really obvious attacks \u2013 lightning bolts, clouds of deadly<br /> gas, and so forth \u2013 are easy to see coming. Invisible ones \u2013<br /> flesh-eating spirits, silent curses, Entropic ripples that collapse<br /> a bridge, that sort of thing \u2013 may be detected with a successful<br /> Perception + Awareness roll, difficulty 8.<br /> &quot;<br /> <br /> So yes: You can dodge 'openly magick' attacks. A lightning bolt from the sky isn't something I imagine most ST's expect players to roll an attack for. (Ironically the blood magick path in Vampire that lets you hit people with lightning requires an aiming roll, I think). Same with a 'silent curse'.<br /> <br /> Also the book implies, rather openly, that you dodge the Arete/Attack/Damage roll as opposed to dodging a normal attack roll (Such as the laster gun)<br /> <br /> Just above the quoted section, 544<br /> <br /> &quot;As detailed under Chapter Nine\u2019s Combat section, a<br /> Dexterity + Athletics (or Acrobatics) roll, difficulty 6, subtracts<br /> successes from an incoming attack. If the attacker still has more<br /> successes than the target, remaining successes determine how<br /> much damage is done\u2026 and if the attacker winds up with only<br /> one success left over, then there\u2019s no damage at all.<br /> &quot;<br /> The one success left over does no damage because 1 success on the magick damage chart = 0 damage (If my memory is correct), so it's directly explaining your dodge cancels out the arete roll. If it was simply an attack roll, the attack would do full damage because the attack roll only needs 1 success to hit and direct damage. A laser gun with 1 success to hit does the same damage as a laser gun with 5 successes to hit, as the damage comes from the following arete roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will contend though: The detecting 'invisible magick/hard to spot magick' section isn't 1000% clear on if you can dodge that spell or if that just lets you know whats going on for countermagick, but I assume it is about dodging magick seeing as it is under the 'dodging physical attacks' section.<br /> <br /> Even if you can't dodge it, you'll be able to know its coming for a countermagick attempt though. I assume that the perception + awareness roll is reflexive and doesn't mess up dice pools. And if you can't do either that's silly as fuck because it just lets me look up a split second before lightning hits me to go &quot;Hm. Welp, fuck&quot;<br /> <br /> The section is worded weirdly because it even starts off like <br /> &quot;Any physical attack (fireball, mystic blade, plasma bolt,<br /> etc.) directed at an essentially solid target (car, person, spirit,<br /> etc.) can be dodged if that target is capable of dodging the<br /> attack in question.<br /> &quot;<br /> So it includes non 'physical attacks' in the 'dodging physical attack' section. *Shrug*. That's whitewolf for ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 11-02-2019, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T00:17:44-07:00","id":1345540,"title":"","content":"Assuming it's a) hostile, b) knows you know it is a vampire, c) not super powerful and d) this is a short term conflict where you are at the same place as the vampire...<br /> <br /> If I was a new character and not specifically made to handle a vampire I'd try to get away from it. Failing that I'd try to calm it down. Even if you're not good at social interaction, you can always beg.<br /> I'd also try to get a hold of the rest of my party as soon as possible.<br /> <br /> General advice:<br /> Always think about what information you need at the moment. Why is the vampire hostile? Is there ways to exit the room? How powerful do the vampire appear to be? Where is your party? If you do manage to exit the room, what ways do you have to leave quickly? Can you steal a car, or get to your own car? On a meta level, how do your gm run kindred? <b>Information defines and provides you options</b><br /> Remember you are a part of a group. Especially when handling a vampire, depend on other pcs. If they aren't dependable, you have a problem for any dangerous situation you are in.<br /> <br /> Other things that can help:<br /> Be careful with mind whammies from the vampire. If you don't have mindwards or do not have strong willpower, at least avoid looking directly at them and listening to them<br /> Forces are decent against kindred. I do not remember what level of forces you need to turn invisible but I think it was 4. Even then though, if you want to get away you could use forces to mute and remove any sounds you make, which might help with stealth roles. Also if you do engage in combat, forces can be used to make some decent invisible armor around yourself (a forcefield), though you might need life 1 to 'lock it' around your pattern since you want it to move with you. Also you might want to do it as a ritual so you get more successes.<br /> <br /> Note also you can just get normal body armor and wear that. This is usually a good idea if you want to engage in violence anyway. The force shield have the advantage of not necessarily being visible though.<br /> <br /> If you want to just snap your finger and set a kindred on fire, you will need not just a paradigm that lets you do that, but also prime 2 in addition to forces, to conjure fire from nothing. Some sts might also decide that you need matter 1 but I don't think it should really be needed. Also it's vulgar so be careful with paradox. If you only have forces, try to carry a lighter around so you can just set things on fire. Also in either case think about the room you are in, and try to not burn down an appartment complex and get a bunch of sleepers killed.<br /> <br /> Other than that you just have your normal selection of combat and escape rotes. Prime 2 lets your attacks deal aggravated damage against supernatural, life keeps you alive, correspondence is great for fleeing but can also make aiming easier, getting into the penumbra with spirits can be useful as well, general physical fitness is good for both dodging and running, matter can quickly help you get trough doors or strengthen doors against people hunting you.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if the kindred appears to be powerful, or if it is not engaging you directly, but trough intermediaries, check if you have a mentor that you can ask to help you. Even if your pc do not have any, check if anyone else in the group has one, or if noone has any, check if you have in game know any npcs in the traditions you can ask for help or advice, or any pull in the traditions and can get them to help you.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> As a side note I honestly do not understand why it'd be any more difficult to jump out of the way of vertical lightning than horizontal lightning.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, the weird freak started to chant a bunch of ooga booga, raise his to the sky, then his chant reached a crescendo and he started to clap his hand together, so I jumped out of the way and then I shot him. He had some forcefields up so he took less damage, but it still looked like it hurt. Serves him right, the damn nerd&quot;<br /> <br /> Though there's a couple of things here that makes the whole thing feel skeevy to me.<br /> <br /> Summoning a lightning bold from the sky seems extremely different from me than most standard forces attacks.<br /> <br /> 1. I'd count the distance of the spell as the highest between either its point of origin and the target, or the mage and the target. So probably you want correspondence two to shift the effect that far up into the sky.<br /> <br /> 2. Generating an actual kilometers long lightning bolt is pretty huge. If a mage wanted to generate a several kilometers long pillar of fire, or a several kilometers long spear out of matter even temporarily, I'd require a large amount of successes. The only difference with lightning in that context is lightning might be coincidental. I'd still require a large amount of successes. I think it'd be easier if they just made sure to check the weather report and go out in the middle of a storm. At that point using forces or entropy to make the poor sod more likely to get hit by lightning seems a lot easier.<br /> <br /> Possible if you had forces 5 and a thematic as a weather wizard I'd wave most of the hoops you need to jump trough and let you automatically call down lightning on people and might even wave their ability to dodge unless they are not mooks. Otherwise you might want to do that specific effect as a ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8754-corioliseffect","user":"CoriolisEffect","date":". 11-03-2019, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8754-corioliseffect","name":"CoriolisEffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T00:45:50-07:00","id":1345545,"title":"","content":"&quot;Forces are decent against kindred. I do not remember what level of forces you need to turn invisible but I think it was 4.&quot; It's forces 2 to wrap light around yourself, you can't see while doing it though without correspondence 1/some other spheres. Forces 2 + life 2 if you want it to make your entire body invisible and not just the small area around you.<br /> <br /> I think making fire without prime 2 and using forces 3 would require Matter 2, as matter 2 is needed for basic transmutation and air ---&gt; fire would qualify. Matter 3 if your ST hates you.<br /> <br /> A lighter + a mouth full of alcohol or even just water + Forces 2 is a very good makeshift fireball though. Coincidental most likely. And a lot more damage than a regular wave of fire ever would be.<br /> <br /> Making invisible armor would require Matter 2 to 'lock it in' properly, not life. It's bound to the armor, not yourself. You'd need life 2 to lock it in to yourself. Locking in stuff requires atleast a 2 in things. Maybe even a 3 <br /> <br /> Matter magick is also powerful. Matter 2-3 (Most likely 3) and Prime 2 (Or just a lot more successes) could be used in a variety of ways to try and slam a stake into a vampire's heart. Maybe you need forces 2 for enough 'force' or just for the extra damage. Turn someone's shirt into a condensed piece of wood that impales them where their heart should be. Or something equally as complicated.<br /> Bonus points if you load this up into a charm and have a ranged way of shooting someone's shirt and having the effect go off to avoid the issue of 'how the fuck do I do this mid combat and get the number of successes needed'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T03:20:51-08:00","id":1345567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345545#post1345545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Forces are decent against kindred. I do not remember what level of forces you need to turn invisible but I think it was 4.&quot; It's forces 2 to wrap light around yourself, you can't see while doing it though without correspondence 1/some other spheres. Forces 2 + life 2 if you want it to make your entire body invisible and not just the small area around you.<br /> <br /> I think making fire without prime 2 and using forces 3 would require Matter 2, as matter 2 is needed for basic transmutation and air ---&gt; fire would qualify. Matter 3 if your ST hates you.<br /> <br /> A lighter + a mouth full of alcohol or even just water + Forces 2 is a very good makeshift fireball though. Coincidental most likely. And a lot more damage than a regular wave of fire ever would be.<br /> <br /> Making invisible armor would require Matter 2 to 'lock it in' properly, not life. It's bound to the armor, not yourself. You'd need life 2 to lock it in to yourself. Locking in stuff requires atleast a 2 in things. Maybe even a 3<br /> <br /> Matter magick is also powerful. Matter 2-3 (Most likely 3) and Prime 2 (Or just a lot more successes) could be used in a variety of ways to try and slam a stake into a vampire's heart. Maybe you need forces 2 for enough 'force' or just for the extra damage. Turn someone's shirt into a condensed piece of wood that impales them where their heart should be. Or something equally as complicated.<br /> Bonus points if you load this up into a charm and have a ranged way of shooting someone's shirt and having the effect go off to avoid the issue of 'how the fuck do I do this mid combat and get the number of successes needed'.</div> </div> </div> </div>You use force to make a forcefield around yourself. It just functions as armor. Since it goes with you when you walk and you are the target and you are alive, you'd need life. If you wanted to lock the forcefield to your jacket you could use matter instead.<br /> <br /> I could see you transmute matter into an elemental force as an alternative to prime, but it seems like an extremely generous st that'd let you apply that to air and have it be effective.<br /> <br /> And you don't need the water or the alcohole unless your paradigm demands it as a focus. Without prime you just need any source of fire, and your foci with forces to throw a fireball at someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8754-corioliseffect","name":"CoriolisEffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T07:56:33-08:00","id":1345592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345513#post1345513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">544, M20<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Really obvious attacks \u2013 lightning bolts, clouds of deadly<br /> gas, and so forth \u2013 are easy to see coming. Invisible ones \u2013<br /> flesh-eating spirits, silent curses, Entropic ripples that collapse<br /> a bridge, that sort of thing \u2013 may be detected with a successful<br /> Perception + Awareness roll, difficulty 8.<br /> &amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So yes: You can dodge 'openly magick' attacks. A lightning bolt from the sky isn't something I imagine most ST's expect players to roll an attack for. (Ironically the blood magick path in Vampire that lets you hit people with lightning requires an aiming roll, I think). Same with a 'silent curse'.<br /> <br /> Also the book implies, rather openly, that you dodge the Arete/Attack/Damage roll as opposed to dodging a normal attack roll (Such as the laster gun)<br /> <br /> Just above the quoted section, 544<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;As detailed under Chapter Nine\u2019s Combat section, a<br /> Dexterity + Athletics (or Acrobatics) roll, difficulty 6, subtracts<br /> successes from an incoming attack. If the attacker still has more<br /> successes than the target, remaining successes determine how<br /> much damage is done\u2026 and if the attacker winds up with only<br /> one success left over, then there\u2019s no damage at all.<br /> &amp;quot;<br /> The one success left over does no damage because 1 success on the magick damage chart = 0 damage (If my memory is correct), so it's directly explaining your dodge cancels out the arete roll. If it was simply an attack roll, the attack would do full damage because the attack roll only needs 1 success to hit and direct damage. A laser gun with 1 success to hit does the same damage as a laser gun with 5 successes to hit, as the damage comes from the following arete roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will contend though: The detecting 'invisible magick/hard to spot magick' section isn't 1000% clear on if you can dodge that spell or if that just lets you know whats going on for countermagick, but I assume it is about dodging magick seeing as it is under the 'dodging physical attacks' section.<br /> <br /> Even if you can't dodge it, you'll be able to know its coming for a countermagick attempt though. I assume that the perception + awareness roll is reflexive and doesn't mess up dice pools. And if you can't do either that's silly as fuck because it just lets me look up a split second before lightning hits me to go &amp;quot;Hm. Welp, fuck&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The section is worded weirdly because it even starts off like <br /> &amp;quot;Any physical attack (fireball, mystic blade, plasma bolt,<br /> etc.) directed at an essentially solid target (car, person, spirit,<br /> etc.) can be dodged if that target is capable of dodging the<br /> attack in question.<br /> &amp;quot;<br /> So it includes non 'physical attacks' in the 'dodging physical attack' section. *Shrug*. That's whitewolf for ya.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the use of dexterity+athletics to describe the attack we can see that M20 is refering to Zeus style literally throwing the lightning bolt like a dart.<br /> This sections clearly refers to spells being used as weapons.<br /> <br /> In page 417, M20 is describing all kind of magickal attacks and tells us that focused magick can be dodged. If openly magickal could it should be stated too.<br /> We also have the &quot;indirect assault&quot; that also can't be dodged. Example is an earthquake, you can't dodge that.<br /> <br /> Instead of throwing (that's the key word that makes the mage roll athletics) a bolt or a fireball, just put fire ln the vampire, or alter the voltage between you and the vampire and an electric arc will be generated just like a real lightning, with the same speed. <br /> <br /> It's not like the mage will create a bolt in his hand, look to the vampire and throw. Everything happens in a turn (3sec), the mage uses his focus and the electrical potential diference increase, making an arc into the vampire instantly. I see no chance of dodge here and the rules, while confusing, seems to support it.<br /> <br /> Also, there is no sense on dodging an Arete roll: an initial mage can have only 3, while a mortal can easily have 6 in dex+dodge up to 10. Getting only 2 successes means no damage for the mage. That's absurd, even normal mortals could avoid damage from mages and that is not what the rules seems to state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T10:15:20-08:00","id":1345609,"title":"","content":"I remember there being a Forces2/Corr2 and Forces 4/Corr 4 rote that opened up a portal to sun to shine it on Vampires. It was in Blood Treachery I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T15:57:33-08:00","id":1345656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoriolisEffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345540#post1345540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces are decent against kindred. I do not remember what level of forces you need to turn invisible but I think it was 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not. Invisibility is Forces 2, because you are bending light away/around you. Invisibility has always been fairly easy (if Vulgar) in Mage, so long as the ST doesn't insist on a &quot;pattern locking&quot; tax related to Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T10:02:59-08:00","id":1347269,"title":"","content":"It would depend on how old the hostile vampire is and what their background might be. I'd be hesitant to go up against even newbie Brujah in hand to hand, but a thin blood or low level Caitiff might be another matter and depending on how much min/max optimizing for that particular situation I'd be allowed to do (which is allowable within the first post I think but also represents a rather... isolated example?) <br /> <br /> The more powerful it is the more inclined I am to go either for 'avoid entirely' or at least 'engage indirectly/at range'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T10:08:09-08:00","id":1347272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vandarl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire#post1345048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I am sure it has been asked before, but my search-fu has failed me. Other than not be in the same city with them, what is the best way for a fresh out of the box Mage to deal with a hostile vampire? Straight chargen, no additional XP. How would you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 3, Prime 2, Mind 1. Forces 3 provides the basis to perform a number of very useful things. First, make yourself invisible to the visible light spectrum (can't hit what you can't see); make yourself levitate over the battlefield (can't hit what you can't reach, even flailing around wildly); reduce gravity in the area and/or levitate target (Celerity and dodging don't mean much if all the target can do is writhe and flail around in one spot.) <b>Caution:</b> direct levitation might be resisted, but it more easily conceptualized, whereas reducing gravity in a small area moves the effect into the category of 'irresistible indirect effects', but may be resisted by some ST's as too amorphous despite HDYDT explicitly stating that this sort of thing is doable with as little as Forces 2. Mind 1 provides the ability to erect a Mind shield and potentially resist or avoid getting Dominated or Presence'd into submission by fledgling with Dominate 1 who has figured out that &quot;Surrender!&quot; is a useful <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentence_word\" target=\"_blank\">one-word sentence</a>.<br /> <br /> So those cover your defense, as well as neutralizing the target's potential defenses. Offense using Forces 3, Prime 2 has been tread so thoroughly above that I won't get into it. Needless to say, if you can sit in your invisible sky bubble to cast for a couple of turns and spend a Willpower, odds are good the vampire's not going to have much for that. Another interesting tactic would be to imbue a firearm with aggravated damage via Prime 2, then put the firearm in an invisible and sound-dampening bubble, then levitate it so that it it's right right behind your target's head, and use telekinesis to pull the trigger. +1000 points for Gryffindor if you use a sawed-off 12-gauge shotgun loaded with buckshot, and aim for the vampire's neck. You're targeting the neck, yes, but you're also firing from pointblank range with a scatter gun. You just need three damage past the soak to decap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1345592#post1345592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there is no sense on dodging an Arete roll: an initial mage can have only 3, while a mortal can easily have 6 in dex+dodge up to 10. Getting only 2 successes means no damage for the mage. That's absurd, even normal mortals could avoid damage from mages and that is not what the rules seems to state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is nonsense. The ease with which one may <i>Dodge </i>(which uses Athletics or Acrobatics) an attack, per the book, depends on factors like how far away the thing being dodged is from the dodger, and how much room the dodger has to move around in space. So without a doubt what is occurring here is that the person is changing their position and location in three-dimensional space to avoid being contacted by a <b>thing</b> which is traveling towards them. It's <i>a priori</i> that being able to perceive a<b> thing</b> is a necessary precondition to reacting purposefully to the <b>thing</b>. While there are plenty of magic attacks that operate in a manner that lend themselves to being perceived and reacted to by most people (and we've named a few), there are plenty of others that absolutely do not work that way.<br /> <br /> If my target and I are facing off, and I use Forces 3 Prime 2 to conjure an invisible laser that originates at an elevated position behind above my target, and approaches my target at a downward 12\u00b0 angle--I don't know how (absent their having magical senses and the like) they're going to know to avoid that. Even if they know I can cast magic, I'm gesturing wildly with one hand and waving a staff with the other, and speaking in tongues... how are they supposed to know where an invisible, inaudible attack is coming from? Well, the game basically provides the equivalent of an Auspex rating because they can roll Perception + Awareness to perceive the attack <i>somehow</i>--and since Awareness is a Talent, at a minimum absolutely <i>everyone </i>is rolling Perception. However, even if I think this is lazy, it's still a game about wizards and vampires, so the fact that everyone on the planet now has <i>the shining </i>for the purposes of dodging true magick (and seemingly only true magick), is as valid as the existence of were hyenas. What I find incongruous is another portion of the very paragraph that describes the Per+Aware rule on pg. 544 of M20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really obvious attacks \u2013 lightning bolts, clouds of deadly gas, and so forth \u2013 are easy to see coming. Invisible ones \u2013 flesh-eating spirits, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>silent curses</b></span>, Entropic ripples that collapse a bridge, that sort of thing \u2013 may be detected with a successful Perception + Awareness roll, difficulty 8. </div> </div> </div>I will readily accept that people will have their sixth sense triggered by having a curse levied against them... but the purpose of this paragraph is to discuss dodging magical effects... so... how do you physically <i>dodge </i>a curse? Are you telling me that if someone is going to curse me with Entropy or Life (i.e., Blight of Aging, or Rip the Man Body, or both), the curse is being literally <i>flung </i>at me, such that if I jump out of the way, someone behind me might get the curse instead? Really? Then why even make a distinction between physical and non-physical in the first place?<br /> <br /> I think one of the big issues with M20 is that they didn't want to futz with the underlying metaphysical mechanics of magic, but they also didn't want mages to be <i>nearly</i> as powerful as they were in previous editions simply by dint of sphere magick giving mages capabilities incomparable to whatever means non-mages have of defending against attacks. So they basically put in rules that dispense with even attempting to make some kind of sense within the metaphysics of the game--in other words, they created escape hatches for non-mages that you have to just accept and not try to make sense of; they're not internally consistent with the rest of the rest of the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 11-09-2019, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T20:24:19-08:00","id":1347389,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2319_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2319\" data-vbnamecard=\"2319\">CaptOtter</a>, I agree with you. M20 has some weird shit rules. But....thay paragraph only talks about detecting a spell. There is no mention about you being able to dodge every spell you detect.<br /> <br /> So, your mage cast a silent curse, the vampire rolls awareness and goes &quot;ok, he's waving hos hands and talking crazy. That mofo is probably going to do something bad with me&quot;. That's it. Next second you curse the hell out of him and that's nothing he can do about it. Same for your invisibe laser. Or the direct electrical arc. It's an openly magickal attack, that is very vulgar, but only uses Arete for the attack and there's no other roll. Aretex2(+1 if Forces) successes on damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T14:00:30-08:00","id":1347551,"title":"","content":"Break into their haven in the middle of the day(quite a few effects help with this) Stake them through the heart. Drag them out into the sun. Have Arcane. Repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T15:46:05-08:00","id":1347566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1347389#post1347389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;2319&quot;]Aretex2(+1 if Forces) successes on damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small correction: It's ( Arete (+1 if forces) ) x2<br /> The forces sphere adds a level of damage - not a point of damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> People also often forget that willpower *adds* a success if used, so an Arete 3 mage could crank out 4 successes on an Arete roll with that. With forces, That's 10 aggravated from a starting mage in a turn. Though it's less likely overall, unless Quintessence is being used to lower difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-10-2019, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T22:39:41-08:00","id":1348413,"title":"","content":"Forces 2 and Correspondence 2. Glorious Sword of Heaven (from Blood Treachery). Just don't let the Massasa know that you are the kind of Mage that uses such spells. Or they will gang up on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T15:45:22-08:00","id":1348953,"title":"","content":"There's always good old ass-kicking.<br /> If you still have to design your mage, but expect a lot of vampire conflict, go full combat monster. It's not widely recommended but you can make a mage close quarters specialist that's rolling 20+ dice of aggravated damage quite easily.<br /> <br /> <b>Take Following: </b><br /> -Physical Primary + Nephilim Merit (or genemods)<br /> -Martial skills + specialty<br /> -Arete 3, LIfe 3+Spirit 3<br /> -Specialized tool to make Fetishes even with spirit 3. Werewolf Paw amulet, anti-magic amulet.<br /> <br /> Make a bunch of short term talens &amp; Fetishes to arm yourself to teeth. Including physical boosts to already ridiculous stats, armor, regen and multiple action. Bind couple Sun spirits.<br /> <br /> You have a complete monster of a vampire hunter with possible support of a couple possessed dogs and spirit assist. It's not even particularly paradox prone, especially if you take a 2-3 points in Blatancy.<br /> Of course MC is also likely a barely human psychopath with bucket load of mutations. But hey, vamps, and basically anything else, will be very dead. very, very dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 11-16-2019, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T19:01:45-08:00","id":1348975,"title":"","content":"And how exactly do you deal 20 dice agg dmg?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T22:59:05-08:00","id":1349286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1348975#post1348975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how exactly do you deal 20 dice agg dmg?</div> </div> </div> </div>Roll around 20 dice, not necessarily deal 20 dice.<br /> <br /> Inhuman physical traits + big ass sword + magic from all kind of fetishes. Let's say you get up to 4 dex/str with starting points, add to it nephilim merit bonus (what is it 5 or 7 points?), get werewolf paw amulet + life magic boost + talen. This will bring you over 10 easily in dex and possibly strength. Then you get more points from just using big enough sword, more dice form making it a short-term fetish (quite easy for month or two duration). If needing more you can always put a deal with war spirits for battle possession and get your skill to 5 and over. And don't forget to make several talens with electricity spirits for multiple actions.<br /> So yeah, u would be rolling ungodly dice pools and as long as you don'g go complete Cu Chulainn it is low on <i>paradox</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 11-18-2019, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T05:15:35-08:00","id":1349314,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's exactly how it works. You can't get multiple actions with Spirit. Also, what makes you think the vampire won't dodge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T06:14:41-08:00","id":1349318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1345048-starting-mage-vs-vampire?p=1349314#post1349314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's exactly how it works. You can't get multiple actions with Spirit. Also, what makes you think the vampire won't dodge?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't get multiple actions with spirit sphere alone, correct. But, you can make one time use charms with spirit sphere of any effect depending on spirit in question. Electricity spirits or wind spirits would be a good choice for such a speed bump.<br /> <br /> Of course vampire can try to dodge, but taking account the primary attribute you buff anyway is dexterity it is unlikely attempt will succeed. Not to mention you aren't really limited in talens to burn for this case, get some hate spirits to auto-guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 11-19-2019, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}